----- SOURCE CODE
-- one.i

            pub fn fn1() { 1 }
            

-- two.i

            pub fn fn2() { 1 }
            

-- main.i

        import one.{fn1}
        import two.{fn2} as one
        

----- ERROR
error: Duplicate import
  ┌─ /src/one/two.i:3:9
  │
2 │         import one.{fn1}
  │         ---------------- First imported here
3 │         import two.{fn2} as one
  │         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Reimported here

`one` has been imported multiple times.
Names in an i module must be unique so one will need to be renamed.
